  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Pasado simple regular:** verbo + **-ed**, igual para todas las personas: *I / she / they visited*.",
      "",
      "**Ortografía**",
      "",
      "- Termina en -e: solo **-d** → *like → liked, dance → danced*.",
      "- Consonante + y: **-ied** → *study → studied*.",
      "- Una sílaba con consonante-vocal-consonante: se duplica → *stop → stopped, plan → planned*.",
      "- Vocal + y: solo -ed → *play → played*.",
      "",
      "**Pronunciación de -ed**",
      "",
      "| Sonido | Cuándo | Ejemplos |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| /t/ | tras sonidos sordos | walked, watched, stopped, cooked |",
      "| /d/ | tras sonidos sonoros | played, cleaned, called |",
      "| /ɪd/ | tras t o d | visited, wanted, needed |",
      "",
      "Truco: la -ed solo añade una sílaba cuando el verbo ya termina en t o d."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I studyed English.",
        "right": "I studied English.",
        "note": "Consonante + y cambia a -ied."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I stoped at a café.",
        "right": "I stopped at a café.",
        "note": "Se duplica la consonante final."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
